            <ArticleTitle>[The determination of left ventricular flow rates using single-probe radiocardiography in the steady-state distribution phase].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>283-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new procedure of extracting data from measurements by single-probe radionuclide ventriculography is presented which reduces the phase differences during summation of single-beat actions and permits the use of a greater number of single actions for summation. Sum curves so determined are better suited for measurements of ejection fractions, compliance and ventricular blood flow rates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
